        "id": "b32edd53-863e-4179-a2d7-5858514fc28e",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Yes — I can see it. An **Xbox Wireless Controller** is connected via Bluetooth and reporting healthy:\n\n- `Xbox Wireless Controller` — Status: OK, Bluetooth\n- `Bluetooth LE XINPUT compatible input device` — OK\n- `XBOX Synthetic Gamepad Bus` — OK (Windows driver stack loaded properly)\n\nSo it's paired and the drivers are live. Quick way to confirm input is working: press the Xbox button and the light should stay solid (not blinking), or check `joy.cpl` (Run → `joy.cpl`) and wiggle the sticks — you should see response there.\n\nOne note: \"old Xbox\" controllers (the original 360-era dongle ones) can be flaky on Win11, but this one enumerated cleanly as a proper XINPUT device, so you're good. Want me to test anything specific — rumble, battery level, or button mapping?",
        "timestamp": 1793192138191,
        "model": "assistant-llm"
      },
