        "id": "a0bb04fb-0e41-4654-bccf-46ff1448a32c",
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "I don't see an Xbox console on this machine. Here's what I checked:\n\n- **No capture card / HDMI-in device** — this PC (Iris Xe laptop-class graphics, Dell S3222HN on HDMI) has no video input, so an Xbox can't feed the PC over HDMI\n- **No Xbox in the device tree** (only the wireless controller from before)\n- **No SSDP/DLNA response** from an Xbox on the LAN\n- **ARP table** — nothing with an obviously Xbox MAC prefix on 192.168.4.x–7.x\n\nSo: how is it actually connected? Possibilities:\n\n1. **HDMI → monitor directly** — if so, I can't see it; the PC has no visibility into the monitor's other inputs\n2. **Over the network** (same Wi-Fi/Ethernet) — I can hunt it down, but nothing responded to discovery. Is the Xbox powered on and on the same network?\n3. **USB** — old consoles (360/original) don't really work over USB for video; only controllers/accessories enumerate\n\nWhat are you trying to do — capture/stream gameplay, or just get files off it? And what model Xbox is it?",
        "timestamp": 1793192279603,
        "model": "assistant-llm"
      },
